      <ID>1000</ID>
      <Description>"Keep Driving v1.3.1.1d  --  ACTIVATE THIS FIRST"</Description>
      <Options moAlwaysHideChildren="1" moAllowManualCollapseAndExpand="1" />
      <Color>2B1CE3</Color>
      <VariableType>Auto Assembler Script</VariableType>
      <AssemblerScript>{ Keep Driving v1.3.1.1d  --  corrected build (v3)

  WHAT THIS TABLE ACTUALLY DOES, MEASURED

  This is a GameMaker (YYC) build. Gameplay values live in a hash map whose heap
  addresses and slot offsets differ on every launch, so static pointer paths are
  useless. What is stable is the code plus the variable-name table in .data, so
  the script below hooks Variable_Get, matches the variable id, and records the
  RValue address from the copy helper underneath it. Rows are pointers to those
  recorded addresses, so they re-aim every launch and freezing follows the value.

  EVERY ROW BELOW WAS TESTED IN A RUNNING GAME. Results:

  CORE - 12 of 12 work. Verified aiming, reading, writing and freezing, and the
  written values were confirmed in savedata.ini after a save. Money's HUD counter
  is repainted lazily so it can lag, but the row does track the wallet.
  Gas Tank Capacity, Energy Max and Car Health Max are session-only - they are not
  stored in the save, and the game recomputes Energy Max when you get tired.

  SITUATIONAL - 11 of 40 populate. They are in the WORKING group, each labelled
  with what it actually reads. The other 29 never populated in any context and are
  parked in the BROKEN group at the bottom rather than left looking usable. 23 of
  those 29 were tested with their own screen open and the value visibly on display
  - a shop tooltip reading 11.25, a garage quoting 55, a glovebox showing 5/5 - and
  the row still read 0. Two of them (item charges, glovebox charges) hold arrays,
  not numbers, so a Double row could never have worked. The remaining 6 could not
  be reached: no work screen and no explore site came up.

  Reviving the BROKEN rows needs a variable-discovery pass, not a better hook. An
  instrumented log of every id the game asks for showed 37 of the 52 ids are never
  requested at all, so those names are not what the game uses for those values. A
  second capture point was built and tested against the slot-lookup return value
  and it did not help: 6.8 million lookups went past it and only gas, energy and
  car health ever matched.

  GAME SPEED - slowing works, speeding up does NOT. Measured against real driving
  (fuel burn per wall-clock second, same road segment, back to back):
      0.25x  -&gt;  0.30x of normal    works
      4x     -&gt;  0.99x and 1.00x    no effect at all, measured twice
  Cheat Engine's speedhack is set correctly in every case - the game simply will
  not run faster than real time. The 2x and 4x entries have been REMOVED because
  they did nothing. 0.5x is kept: same mechanism as the measured 0.25x, but it was
  not separately measured.


  AUTOMATIC POINTER FINDER  (the entry directly under this script)

  The script above can only fill a row once the game happens to READ that
  variable, which is why so many rows sat at 0. The finder does not wait. It
  captures the stats object, walks the variable hash map inside it, and writes
  each variable's live address straight into the slot this script allocated:

      object + 0x48  -&gt; hash map        map + 0x08 -&gt; bucket mask
      map + 0x10     -&gt; bucket array    16 bytes per entry
      entry + 0x00   -&gt; RValue*         entry + 0x0C -&gt; (varid + 1), bit 31 clear
      RValue: value at +0, kind at +12  (0 = number, 2 = array)

  Enable the main script first, then enable AUTO-FIND POINTERS. It re-runs every
  2 seconds, so rows re-aim by themselves after a load or a restart.

  What it changes, measured: 21 rows are resolved the moment a save is loaded,
  with no gameplay at all - including three that the hook could never reach.
  Gas drain rate is now live and was verified end to end: setting it to 0 took
  fuel burn from 0.0349 gas/s to 0.0000 while driving. Cost modifier - gas and
  Cost modifier - energy also populate.

  It does NOT revive everything. 29 of the 52 variables are not in the stats
  object at all, so they stay dead until someone finds which object owns them.
  Two more (ailment timer and duration) are arrays rather than numbers, so the
  finder deliberately skips them instead of writing a garbage pointer into a
  Double row.

  USEFUL COMBINATIONS

  - Freeze Clock-Hour and Calendar-Day to stop time and quest deadlines. Verified:
    the dash clock stops while fuel keeps draining.
  - Raise Gas Tank Capacity BEFORE Gas, and Car Health Max / Energy Max before
    their values, or the needle runs off the dial. Raising the maxima visibly
    grows the dashboard gauges.

  Tested 2026-08-28 against KeepDriving.exe v1.3.1.1d (30,260,736 bytes) across
  full restarts, driving, road events, the shop, the fuel pump, the trunk, the
  glovebox, the map and a garage.

  ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Altxxr0        https://github.com/altxxr0/KeepDrivingCE
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------

}

[ENABLE]
{$lua}
if syntaxcheck then return end
